nio: mark parse_machfile in the boot's first execve

The panel now reaches exec_mach_imgact and "machfile: halt init task",
then stops before any further mark.  The next substantial call in
load_machfile is parse_machfile(), which copyins the Mach-O header and maps
the segments into the init task's map -- the exact place a copyout/copyin
into the half-initialised init map could stall.

  nio: ML pre-parse-machfile / parse args vp map off size
  nio: ML post-parse-machfile lret=N

pre without post means parse_machfile is the blocking call. Diagnosis only.

diff --git a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
--- a/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/mach_loader.c
@@ -588,9 +588,13 @@
 	result->is_64bit_addr = ((imgp->ip_flags & IMGPF_IS_64BIT_ADDR) == IMGPF_IS_64BIT_ADDR);
 	result->is_64bit_data = ((imgp->ip_flags & IMGPF_IS_64BIT_DATA) == IMGPF_IS_64BIT_DATA);
 
+	printf("\nnio: ML pre-parse-machfile\n");
+	printf("nio: ML parse args vp=%p map=%p off=%lld size=%lld\n", (void*)vp, (void*)map,
+	    (long long)file_offset, (long long)macho_size);
 	lret = parse_machfile(vp, map, thread, header, file_offset, macho_size,
 	    0, aslr_page_offset, dyld_aslr_page_offset, result,
 	    NULL, imgp);
+	printf("nio: ML post-parse-machfile lret=%d\n", (int)lret);
 
 	if (lret != LOAD_SUCCESS) {
 		vm_map_deallocate(map); /* will lose pmap reference too */
